f smaller pieces. Something like Polaris has a tight, consistent design because of this, and you can feel how each component has had a lot of thought and effort behind it.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I hadn’t known about this approach until recently, which is known by some as “atomic design”. When I was learning about UI and UX a few years back, I genuinely thought that designs systems were born out of a product, not the other way round. You would design your product first, then break it down to the component level to create your design system.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Looking at what I used to do when designing apps or tools, it seems crazy to me that I wasn’t doing this. It makes so much sense from a consistency and development point of view, and it’s evident in my early work that this was affecting me (although at the time I did not know this).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I love the idea of developing a mini design system that I can utilise for various web projects. I feel as though having the added restriction of only being able to use a select set of components would actually open up a lot of creative possibilities, and would also (hopefully) result in me being able to finish things faster.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Let’s see how it goes.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'On the idea of a creative design system', NULL, 'Thinking about ways to test my components in isolation.', '2024-09-16T12:00:00.000Z', 0, 'on-the-idea-of-a-creative-design-system', '2025-10-24T06:56:07.302Z', '2025-10-24T06:54:49.282Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T06:56:08.118Z', '2025-10-24T06:56:08.118Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (24, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-10-24T07:06:40.518Z', '2025-10-24T07:06:40.515Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:06:40.616Z', '2025-10-24T07:06:40.616Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (25, 10, 'This is a test', NULL, NULL, 'This is a test', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'this-is-a-test', '2025-10-24T07:06:56.765Z', '2025-10-24T07:06:40.515Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:06:56.765Z', '2025-10-24T07:06:56.765Z', 1, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (26, 11, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-10-24T07:15:11.039Z', '2025-10-24T07:15:11.037Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:15:11.451Z', '2025-10-24T07:15:11.451Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (27, 11, NULL, NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Before I forget, I wanted to reflect on a few key moments from 2023.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"At the start of the year, I got married to my best friend in the entire world. Surrounded by family and friends, it turned out to be an awesome day. We were both grateful for how the wedding turned out, and it will remain to be the happiest moment of my life. I grateful to everyone who came and spent the day celebrating with us.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"When I returned to work I did a lot of work migrating the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043b7","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://learn.tewahi.com/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Te Wāhi Learn","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":"website onto a new version of ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043b8","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://nextra.site/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Nextra","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". I used the opportunity to add new content and courses onto the site, and develop new tools that could help my students make art (","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043b9","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.anzaaeresources.nz/collections/te-wahi-auaha-at-takapuna-grammar/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Robin and I did a talk about this at ASATA","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":"). I’m proud of the work we did, and of my ability to do this with my limited understanding of Javascript and web development. I’m hoping I can train myself in this area in the new year.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In July, I left my job at Takapuna Grammar School and relocated to Wellington with my wife. While it was hard to move away from my family and friends, it was exciting to move to a new place and set ourselves up from scratch. We filled our Honda Fit with all our belongings and drove to our new home, trying not to bottom out the car along state highway one.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"A few months into my new job in Wellington, I picked up web analytics for the first time. While I dislike ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043ba","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stallman.org/google.html","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Google and their practices","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", I appreciated being able to learn how to use GA4 and Looker Studio to visualise analytics data. In the future, I would love to work more in this space using more privacy respecting tools such as ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043bb","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://plausible.io/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Plausible","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"We spent Christmas and New Year’s between our respective families. I got to spend a lot of time with my nieces, visiting playgrounds and parks around Auckland. Even in the few months we’ve been away they’ve grown an incredible amount.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I don’t have any New Year’s resolutions at the moment besides the typical things one wishes they can do more of. We want to spend more time travelling next year, and I want to continue learning and making new things. We are hoping later in the year we can go to Japan to see my family and friends there.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', '2023 highlights', NULL, 'A reflection on 2023. ', '2023-12-30T11:00:00.000Z', 1, NULL, '2025-10-24T07:17:30.721Z', '2025-10-24T07:15:11.037Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:16:41.054Z', '2025-10-24T07:17:30.721Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (28, 11, '2023 highlights', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Before I forget, I wanted to reflect on a few key moments from 2023.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"At the start of the year, I got married to my best friend in the entire world. Surrounded by family and friends, it turned out to be an awesome day. We were both grateful for how the wedding turned out, and it will remain to be the happiest moment of my life. I grateful to everyone who came and spent the day celebrating with us.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"When I returned to work I did a lot of work migrating the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043b7","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://learn.tewahi.com/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Te Wāhi Learn","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":"website onto a new version of ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043b8","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://nextra.site/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Nextra","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". I used the opportunity to add new content and courses onto the site, and develop new tools that could help my students make art (","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043b9","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.anzaaeresources.nz/collections/te-wahi-auaha-at-takapuna-grammar/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Robin and I did a talk about this at ASATA","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":"). I’m proud of the work we did, and of my ability to do this with my limited understanding of Javascript and web development. I’m hoping I can train myself in this area in the new year.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In July, I left my job at Takapuna Grammar School and relocated to Wellington with my wife. While it was hard to move away from my family and friends, it was exciting to move to a new place and set ourselves up from scratch. We filled our Honda Fit with all our belongings and drove to our new home, trying not to bottom out the car along state highway one.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"A few months into my new job in Wellington, I picked up web analytics for the first time. While I dislike ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043ba","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stallman.org/google.html","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Google and their practices","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", I appreciated being able to learn how to use GA4 and Looker Studio to visualise analytics data. In the future, I would love to work more in this space using more privacy respecting tools such as ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb27cff68b7cd126f043bb","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://plausible.io/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Plausible","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"We spent Christmas and New Year’s between our respective families. I got to spend a lot of time with my nieces, visiting playgrounds and parks around Auckland. Even in the few months we’ve been away they’ve grown an incredible amount.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I don’t have any New Year’s resolutions at the moment besides the typical things one wishes they can do more of. We want to spend more time travelling next year, and I want to continue learning and making new things. We are hoping later in the year we can go to Japan to see my family and friends there.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', '2023 highlights', NULL, 'A reflection on 2023. ', '2023-12-30T11:00:00.000Z', 0, '2023-highlights', '2025-10-24T07:18:04.038Z', '2025-10-24T07:15:11.037Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T07:18:04.836Z', '2025-10-24T07:18:04.836Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (29, 12, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-10-24T07:26:01.632Z', '2025-10-24T07:26:01.632Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:26:02.040Z', '2025-10-24T07:26:02.040Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (30, 12, 'My first developer job', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"While I’ve been helping out on small pieces here and there on top of my normal day job, two months ago I “officially” became a software developer full time.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It is something that always in the back of my mind since I was in high school, but I never pursued it seriously as I felt I wasn’t smart enough. Even the past few years where I have mostly written web apps and tools for fun, I’d always figured I was too late - that since I hadn’t started learning in my early twenties or teens that there was no point in trying.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Out of the blue I was suddenly offered the role, doing mostly stuff I had already been doing on the side with Next.js, Typescript and Express but in an official capacity. I’m hugely thankful for the opportunity, and in particular the help and support from my colleagues who have pushed me to pursue this and back myself.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I am not really sure if I should shout them out in person here, don’t really know what the proper etiquette is. But in any case, it is thanks to them that I decided to start taking this seriously and pursue it as a career. I’ll be forever grateful to them for believing in me.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I still feel like an imposter now, but I suspect I always will which is okay as the uncertainty has always helped to motivate me to learn and get better (or at least to a point where I can say I’m “good enough”). I thought for the longest time in my teens and twenties that I would be an artist since that is all I knew and thought I was good at, but it turns out it is never too late to try something new.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'My first developer job', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 'my-first-developer-job', '2025-10-24T07:26:48.490Z', '2025-10-24T07:26:01.632Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:26:18.626Z', '2025-10-24T07:26:48.490Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (31, 12, 'My first developer job', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"While I’ve been helping out on small pieces here and there on top of my normal day job, two months ago I “officially” became a software developer full time.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It is something that always in the back of my mind since I was in high school, but I never pursued it seriously as I felt I wasn’t smart enough. Even the past few years where I have mostly written web apps and tools for fun, I’d always figured I was too late - that since I hadn’t started learning in my early twenties or teens that there was no point in trying.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Out of the blue I was suddenly offered the role, doing mostly stuff I had already been doing on the side with Next.js, Typescript and Express but in an official capacity. I’m hugely thankful for the opportunity, and in particular the help and support from my colleagues who have pushed me to pursue this and back myself.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I am not really sure if I should shout them out in person here, don’t really know what the proper etiquette is. But in any case, it is thanks to them that I decided to start taking this seriously and pursue it as a career. I’ll be forever grateful to them for believing in me.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I still feel like an imposter now, but I suspect I always will which is okay as the uncertainty has always helped to motivate me to learn and get better (or at least to a point where I can say I’m “good enough”). I thought for the longest time in my teens and twenties that I would be an artist since that is all I knew and thought I was good at, but it turns out it is never too late to try something new.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'My first developer job', NULL, 'For the past two months, I’ve been working full time as a developer. ', '2025-04-04T11:00:00.000Z', 0, 'my-first-developer-job', '2025-10-24T07:27:06.259Z', '2025-10-24T07:26:01.632Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T07:27:07.066Z', '2025-10-24T07:27:07.066Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (32, 13, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-10-24T07:28:00.775Z', '2025-10-24T07:28:00.775Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:28:01.181Z', '2025-10-24T07:28:01.181Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (33, 13, 'New rewrite', NULL, NULL, 'New rewrite', NULL, 'I recently made the switch to Next.js.', NULL, 1, 'new-rewrite', '2025-10-24T07:28:31.861Z', '2025-10-24T07:28:00.775Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:28:17.102Z', '2025-10-24T07:28:31.861Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (34, 13, 'New rewrite', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After nearly 4 years of using 11ty as my static site generator, I decided to bite the bullet and give Next.js a try.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The 11ty site I had been using was originally a portfolio starter template by Piper Haywood and Sam Baldwin, the former who was kind enough to talk to me in 2020 and gave me advice on how to get started with web work as a complete newbie.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I have been using Next for a number of products that we have been building at work, so felt comfortable enough to give it a try for this site rewrite. The flexibility offered by Next and React is what got me interested in the first place. My original website wasn''t particularly feature-rich or complicated to begin with, so it wouldn''t be too difficult to try recreate this.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Having migrated all of my content and work across, the site feels noticeable faster compared to 11ty. While 11ty build times are still much, much faster by comparison, this doesn''t really affect the end user experience. Vercel takes care of the deployment, and next/image ensures that all of my images are optimised when they are sent to the viewer which is awesome.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In the future, I want to expand the functionality of this site by creating more custom components and libraries. For example, all of the Are.na channels that I have are being rendered as iframes, so it would be great if I could leverage something like arena-ts so that this loads natively with proper image optimisation. Since iframes aren''t particularly accessible and are difficult to navigate using a keyboard, this would be a big plus as well.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you''re interested in seeing the code, feel free to take a look on my GitHub.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'New rewrite', NULL, 'I recently made the switch to Next.js.', '2024-06-26T12:00:00.000Z', 0, 'new-rewrite', '2025-10-24T07:28:58.768Z', '2025-10-24T07:28:00.775Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T07:28:59.577Z', '2025-10-24T07:28:59.577Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (35, 13, 'New rewrite', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After nearly 4 years of using 11ty as my static site generator, I decided to bite the bullet and give Next.js a try.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The 11ty site I had been using was originally a portfolio starter template by Piper Haywood and Sam Baldwin, the former who was kind enough to talk to me in 2020 and gave me advice on how to get started with web work as a complete newbie.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I have been using Next for a number of products that we have been building at work, so felt comfortable enough to give it a try for this site rewrite. The flexibility offered by Next and React is what got me interested in the first place. My original website wasn''t particularly feature-rich or complicated to begin with, so it wouldn''t be too difficult to try recreate this.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Having migrated all of my content and work across, the site feels noticeable faster compared to 11ty. While 11ty build times are still much, much faster by comparison, this doesn''t really affect the end user experience. Vercel takes care of the deployment, and next/image ensures that all of my images are optimised when they are sent to the viewer which is awesome.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In the future, I want to expand the functionality of this site by creating more custom components and libraries. For example, all of the Are.na channels that I have are being rendered as iframes, so it would be great if I could leverage something like arena-ts so that this loads natively with proper image optimisation. Since iframes aren''t particularly accessible and are difficult to navigate using a keyboard, this would be a big plus as well.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you''re interested in seeing the code, feel free to take a look on my GitHub.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'New rewrite', NULL, 'I recently made the switch to Next.js.', '2024-06-26T12:00:00.000Z', 0, 'new-rewrite', '2025-10-24T07:29:21.233Z', '2025-10-24T07:28:00.775Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T07:29:22.050Z', '2025-10-24T07:29:22.050Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (36, 5, 'North Virginia is for lovers (of cascading failures)', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"So chances are you have already read about this, but from about 9pm last night I began to experience issues with logging into a bunch of services online. Turns out it was the early signs of what would become a major outage with the us-east-1 AWS region that would take out a bunch of different popular services (including Strapi Cloud, which I use for this blog lol).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It''s made me reflect on AWS as a whole. I''ve been learning about different AWS products and microservice architectures in general over the past year, as this is our primary approach with the tools and services we write at work. At this point, we are fully locked into AWS and ap-southeast-2 is our mothership. I am rolling with the big boys, so it is about time I learned how to play the game and get in line.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"While we at work don''t have any reason to deploy things in North Virginia, if there was ever a Sydney or Auckland outage we would be pretty fucked. We rely on all the popular AWS products and it makes sense - I really like using most of them in isolation like DynamoDB, Lambdas and so on. But when you start to abstract away literally everything into a million pieces, and then need a literal certification to be able to understand the 4D \"UX\" patterns of AWS then surely something is wrong. There''s no reason given the design of the internet that all these services should have gone out today because a single provider and their load balancer health check had an existential crisis (I am oversimplifying here ... just let me rant lol).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This comment that I saw on Hacker News describes this well in my opinion:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"\"The costs, performance overhead, and complexity of a modern AWS deployment are insane and so out of line with what most companies should be taking on. But hype + microservices + sunk cost, and here we are.\" - Rob Sanheim","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"68fb211d86ce791a46ac0c3a","media":6,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Seems like a catch-22 in my mind. I can see the appeal of AWS scale if you as a business/company reach a certain scale - that yummy elastic compute makes a lot of sense. At the same time, at that same size the costs on your public clouds like AWS/GCP/Azure etc start to get insanely expensive. Just look at someone like 37 Signals / DHH, who has saved approximately $3.2 million USD moving from AWS to bare-metal, and did not experience any downtime because of a hiccup in North Virginia ...","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'North Virginia is for lovers (of cascading failures)', NULL, 'I dropped the us-east-1 basket and broke all the eggs', '2025-10-20T11:00:00.000Z', 0, 'north-virginia-is-for-lovers-of-cascading-failures', '2025-10-24T07:29:54.083Z', '2025-10-24T06:44:24.364Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:29:54.083Z', '2025-10-24T07:29:54.083Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (37, 5, 'North Virginia is for lovers (of cascading failures)', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"So chances are you have already read about this, but from about 9pm last night I began to experience issues with logging into a bunch of services online. Turns out it was the early signs of what would become a major outage with the us-east-1 AWS region that would take out a bunch of different popular services (including Strapi Cloud, which I use for this blog lol).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It''s made me reflect on AWS as a whole. I''ve been learning about different AWS products and microservice architectures in general over the past year, as this is our primary approach with the tools and services we write at work. At this point, we are fully locked into AWS and ap-southeast-2 is our mothership. I am rolling with the big boys, so it is about time I learned how to play the game and get in line.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"While we at work don''t have any reason to deploy things in North Virginia, if there was ever a Sydney or Auckland outage we would be pretty fucked. We rely on all the popular AWS products and it makes sense - I really like using most of them in isolation like DynamoDB, Lambdas and so on. But when you start to abstract away literally everything into a million pieces, and then need a literal certification to be able to understand the 4D \"UX\" patterns of AWS then surely something is wrong. There''s no reason given the design of the internet that all these services should have gone out today because a single provider and their load balancer health check had an existential crisis (I am oversimplifying here ... just let me rant lol).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This comment that I saw on Hacker News describes this well in my opinion:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"\"The costs, performance overhead, and complexity of a modern AWS deployment are insane and so out of line with what most companies should be taking on. But hype + microservices + sunk cost, and here we are.\" ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"- Rob Sanheim","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":2},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"68fb211d86ce791a46ac0c3a","media":6,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Seems like a catch-22 in my mind. I can see the appeal of AWS scale if you as a business/company reach a certain scale - that yummy elastic compute makes a lot of sense. At the same time, at that same size the costs on your public clouds like AWS/GCP/Azure etc start to get insanely expensive. Just look at someone like 37 Signals / DHH, who has saved approximately $3.2 million USD moving from AWS to bare-metal, and did not experience any downtime because of a hiccup in North Virginia.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'North Virginia is for lovers (of cascading failures)', NULL, 'I dropped the us-east-1 basket and broke all the eggs', '2025-10-20T11:00:00.000Z', 0, 'north-virginia-is-for-lovers-of-cascading-failures', '2025-10-24T07:30:13.362Z', '2025-10-24T06:44:24.364Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T07:30:14.173Z', '2025-10-24T07:30:14.173Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (38, 14, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-10-24T07:30:31.174Z', '2025-10-24T07:30:31.174Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:30:31.577Z', '2025-10-24T07:30:31.577Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (39, 14, 'Carterton', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"68fb2b423fff295afb4677cb","media":8,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', NULL, NULL, 'An image of the lavender farms in Carterton, Wellington.', NULL, 1, 'carterton', '2025-10-24T07:31:43.793Z', '2025-10-24T07:30:31.174Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:30:49.629Z', '2025-10-24T07:31:43.793Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (40, 14, 'Carterton', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"68fb2b423fff295afb4677cb","media":8,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', NULL, NULL, 'An image of the lavender farms in Carterton, Wellington.', '2024-01-13T11:00:00.000Z', 0, 'carterton', '2025-10-24T07:31:49.555Z', '2025-10-24T07:30:31.174Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T07:31:50.368Z', '2025-10-24T07:31:50.368Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (41, 9, 'On the idea of a creative design system', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"One of the things we do at work we writing new UI components is create unit tests and stories to validate + illustrate the functionality of what we’ve created.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It works well as a process, since it forces us to think about how components could be reused across different apps and not have it defined by specific business logic. This encourages components to be reused in the future, rather than having to reinvent the wheel with each new project.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"There are many mature examples of this in different design systems. Polaris by Shopify is one such example, which is still tightly coupled with Shopify as a product but allows anyone to see each component as a sum of smaller pieces. Something like Polaris has a tight, consistent design because of this, and you can feel how each component has had a lot of thought and effort behind it.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I hadn’t known about this approach until recently, which is known by some as “atomic design”. When I was learning about UI and UX a few years back, I genuinely thought that designs systems were born out of a product, not the other way round. You would design your product first, then break it down to the component level to create your design system.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Looking at what I used to do when designing apps or tools, it seems crazy to me that I wasn’t doing this. It makes so much sense from a consistency and development point of view, and it’s evident in my early work that this was affecting me (although at the time I did not know this).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I love the idea of developing a mini design system that I can utilise for various web projects. I feel as though having the added restriction of only being able to use a select set of components would actually open up a lot of creative possibilities, and would also (hopefully) result in me being able to finish things faster.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Let’s see how it goes.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'On the idea of a creative design system', NULL, 'Thinking about ways to test my components in isolation.', '2024-09-16T12:00:00.000Z', 0, 'on-the-idea-of-a-creative-design-system', '2025-10-24T07:32:42.398Z', '2025-10-24T06:54:49.282Z', 'published', '2025-10-24T07:32:43.189Z', '2025-10-24T07:32:43.189Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (42, 15, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-10-24T07:33:27.378Z', '2025-10-24T07:33:27.378Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:33:27.782Z', '2025-10-24T07:33:27.782Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (43, 15, 'Elmet Brae', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Some of us from ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677cc","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://merveilles.town","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Merveilles","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", a loose collective that I''ve been part of for a while now, recently released a compilation of noise/drone/ambient music inspired by the idea of \"the land\", released for free via ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677cd","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://orllewin.github.io/elmet_brae/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Elmet Brae records","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677ce","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://beldamrecords.bandcamp.com/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Beldam","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"While I''ve worked with Merveilles on other projects before, this is the first one I''ve done involving sound/music. My contribution is pretty small, but it was a great thing to get involved with and a way of me connecting to ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677cf","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://tom.so/posts/wee-tour-of-p%C5%8Dneke/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"where I now call home","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"More details about each track and artist can be found on ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677d0","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://orllewin.github.io/elmet_brae/EB01/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"the dedicated microsite","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" set up by ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677d1","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://orllewin.github.io/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Gogledd Orllewin","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". Album art was created by the talented ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677d2","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://nchrs.xyz/","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Rostiger","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Note: if you do end up liking this, please download it once and listen locally. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"68fb2c013fff295afb4677d3","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://archive.is/7DuT5","newTab":false,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Music streaming is not sustainable","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", and it is always better to have your own copy :)","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Elmet Brae', NULL, 'Some of us from Merveilles recently released a compilation of music inspired by the idea of the land.', NULL, 1, 'elmet-brae', '2025-10-24T07:34:35.605Z', '2025-10-24T07:33:27.378Z', 'draft', '2025-10-24T07:33:53.514Z', '2025-10-24T07:34:35.605Z', 0, 1);
