l":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This book came out in late 2016. At that time, I was still working and making collaboratively, and had a made few “successful” works that both pissed a lot of people off as well as registered commercial interest. We didn’t really know what we were doing, but I think there was a lot of naivety and arrogance on our part thinking that this balance of making engaging work and making money was “easy”.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"We got really far, but ultimately I found out the hard way that this world wasn’t really for me and I turned away from it completely. Since then I have made a few small things here and there, but have largely turned my back on making from the hurt that I experienced when I was younger. I said yes to a lot of things which I probably should’ve said no, but I suppose that is the benefit of hindsight.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Things might have turned out a bit differently if I had read this book in 2016. I could have learned about how someone like David Hammons had dealt with similar issues - that you can step back from all the nonsense but continue to engage in a critical and meaningful way without selling yourself away. You don’t have to give up on making completely, and if anything poke fun at the enormous power imbalance that exists in the industry (and probably always will).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6900971c36105819bbe45c4b","media":18,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"At this point I don’t know if I will ever engage in the art world ever again, or even try to make “art” in the same way. I’ll probably always be working on small things, but never for the purpose of a gallery circuit or something similar. I used to feel quite cut about this but I think I’ve found other things to occupy myself. The art world and its creatures helped me learn about different things that have shaped how I conduct myself in a broader sense which has probably been the most productive thing. If anything, it actually taught me very little about art making lol.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Tell them I said no', NULL, 'A book I should have read years ago. ', '2025-10-28T09:00:00.000Z', 0, 'tell-them-i-said-no', '2025-10-30T07:52:38.572Z', '2025-10-28T09:55:08.009Z', 'published', '2025-10-30T07:52:39.378Z', '2025-10-30T07:52:39.378Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (66, 20, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-11-16T10:22:31.636Z', '2025-11-16T10:22:31.633Z', 'draft', '2025-11-16T10:22:31.688Z', '2025-11-16T10:22:31.688Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (67, 20, 'In praise of tinkering', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I''ve been using Linux distributions as my primary operating system since I was a teenager in highschool. I''d saved $450 of my hard earned pocket money, and bought a second-hand Sony Vaio Core 2 Duo machine from NZ Daisuki (better known as \"Japanese Trade Me\" in my family). ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6919a7a03296eba8dbdb9559","media":20,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I was so excited. Finally my own computer, I can download and run whatever software I want! It came with Windows 7 preinstalled, so I preceded to customise it with all kinds of third party skins and themes from Zedge and pasted all kinds of registry hacks from YouTube tutorials to try get the most out of this machine. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It was fun for a while, but it wasn''t long before Microsoft started to complain. I was technically running an outdated version of Windows 7, but each successive update made my machine incredibly slow, and it appeared that the future of Windows was that of Metro UI - flat, touch friendly interface with very little customisation available. I didn''t want to lose this awesome and crazy hacked OS, but having an outdated, unsupported system was also starting to worry me. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6919a6c33296eba8dbdb9558","media":19,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Then by pure chance, I happened upon a desktop image on Tumblr of a Ubuntu system running i3 window manager with a Touhou background. It was about as weeb as you could get, but I loved how personalised it was and immediately wanted to find out more. What was a window manager? Xorg? i3-gaps? I was fascinated by this new rabbit hole I''d opened up. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The rest is probably quite similar to how a lot of people like to personalise their Linux machines. I knew nothing when it came to using a package manager, using a terminal etc and it was obviously far before LLMs, so I spent countless hours on Stackoverflow and the Arch Linux wiki trying to tinker. It was so frustrating, with several of my endeavours leading to kernel panics and completely messed up boot loaders, but boy did I have fun. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Little did I know that my pursuit in making the \"ultimate Linux system\" resulted in me learning about how Linux and Unix-like systems work, basic shell scripting, and networking. Soon enough I was also tinkering on hobby VPS boxes, learning about LAMP, hosting small Wordpress and Discourse instances for my friends, and feeling increasingly like the world was my oyster with respect to computers. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It was all thanks to that old Sony Vaio laptop, which still works to this day (although now runs Slackware) and the fact that I had such a dogshit experience with Microsoft that I started tinkering with computers. I credit it in part with me ending up as a software developer much later on in life and for fuelling my creativity where all other avenues ran dry. Messing around with alternative operating systems like Linux (and some BSDs) made my experience with these machines felt so real. If I entered a bad command or mucked up some kind of Nginx rule, it would be my fault and that was awesome. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The weird thing is that I miss administering Linux boxes that could completely shit the bed if I misconfigured something. These are all \"bad\" things but they felt REAL. I felt like I was in a feedback loop with my machine. I knew when I made a mistake, and could immediately learn as to what I''d done wrong. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"What seemed like endless troubleshooting of my own fuck ups was in fact a series of invaluable lessons on debugging and learning to be a good developer. In most other pursuits like art or sports I would grow frustrated and impatient, but for whatever reason the computer just never stopped being interesting. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It is probably the case for most things in life now, but I do wish failure was more socially acceptable. I failed countless times over the years using Linux, but I''ve learned so much as a result. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"That''s the real point, I think. I''m incredibly grateful for the mess and freedom I had to tinker. I was looking for a way to have a \"computer that could do cool shit\", one that I could show off to my friends in high school, and ended up with a career in making computers do cool shit lol. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'In praise of tinkering', NULL, 'A wee love letter to Linux', '2025-11-16T09:00:00.000Z', 1, 'in-praise-of-tinkering', '2025-11-16T10:31:22.350Z', '2025-11-16T10:22:31.633Z', 'draft', '2025-11-16T10:22:46.446Z', '2025-11-16T10:31:22.350Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (68, 20, 'In praise of tinkering', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I''ve been using Linux distributions as my primary operating system since I was a teenager in highschool. I''d saved $450 of my hard earned pocket money, and bought a second-hand Sony Vaio Core 2 Duo machine from NZ Daisuki (better known as \"Japanese Trade Me\" in my family). ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6919a7a03296eba8dbdb9559","media":20,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I was so excited. Finally my own computer, I can download and run whatever software I want! It came with Windows 7 preinstalled, so I preceded to customise it with all kinds of third party skins and themes from Zedge and pasted all kinds of registry hacks from YouTube tutorials to try get the most out of this machine. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It was fun for a while, but it wasn''t long before Microsoft started to complain. I was technically running an outdated version of Windows 7, but each successive update made my machine incredibly slow, and it appeared that the future of Windows was that of Metro UI - flat, touch friendly interface with very little customisation available. I didn''t want to lose this awesome and crazy hacked OS, but having an outdated, unsupported system was also starting to worry me. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6919a6c33296eba8dbdb9558","media":19,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Then by pure chance, I happened upon a desktop image on Tumblr of a Ubuntu system running i3 window manager with a Touhou background. It was about as weeb as you could get, but I loved how personalised it was and immediately wanted to find out more. What was a window manager? Xorg? i3-gaps? I was fascinated by this new rabbit hole I''d opened up. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The rest is probably quite similar to how a lot of people like to personalise their Linux machines. I knew nothing when it came to using a package manager, using a terminal etc and it was obviously far before LLMs, so I spent countless hours on Stackoverflow and the Arch Linux wiki trying to tinker. It was so frustrating, with several of my endeavours leading to kernel panics and completely messed up boot loaders, but boy did I have fun. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Little did I know that my pursuit in making the \"ultimate Linux system\" resulted in me learning about how Linux and Unix-like systems work, basic shell scripting, and networking. Soon enough I was also tinkering on hobby VPS boxes, learning about LAMP, hosting small Wordpress and Discourse instances for my friends, and feeling increasingly like the world was my oyster with respect to computers. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It was all thanks to that old Sony Vaio laptop, which still works to this day (although now runs Slackware) and the fact that I had such a dogshit experience with Microsoft that I started tinkering with computers. I credit it in part with me ending up as a software developer much later on in life and for fuelling my creativity where all other avenues ran dry. Messing around with alternative operating systems like Linux (and some BSDs) made my experience with these machines felt so real. If I entered a bad command or mucked up some kind of Nginx rule, it would be my fault and that was awesome. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The weird thing is that I miss administering Linux boxes that could completely shit the bed if I misconfigured something. These are all \"bad\" things but they felt REAL. I felt like I was in a feedback loop with my machine. I knew when I made a mistake, and could immediately learn as to what I''d done wrong. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"What seemed like endless troubleshooting of my own fuck ups was in fact a series of invaluable lessons on debugging and learning to be a good developer. In most other pursuits like art or sports I would grow frustrated and impatient, but for whatever reason the computer just never stopped being interesting. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"It is probably the case for most things in life now, but I do wish failure was more socially acceptable. I failed countless times over the years using Linux, but I''ve learned so much as a result. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"That''s the real point, I think. I''m incredibly grateful for the mess and freedom I had to tinker. I was looking for a way to have a \"computer that could do cool shit\", one that I could show off to my friends in high school, and ended up with a career in making computers do cool shit lol. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'In praise of tinkering', NULL, 'A wee love letter to Linux', '2025-11-16T09:00:00.000Z', 0, 'in-praise-of-tinkering', '2025-11-16T10:31:24.878Z', '2025-11-16T10:22:31.633Z', 'published', '2025-11-16T10:31:24.900Z', '2025-11-16T10:31:24.900Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (69, 21, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-11-24T10:24:36.155Z', '2025-11-24T10:24:36.153Z', 'draft', '2025-11-24T10:24:36.173Z', '2025-11-24T10:24:36.173Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (70, 22, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-11-27T02:41:16.044Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.042Z', 'draft', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.061Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.061Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (71, 22, 'Stainless is amazing', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Recently I created a hobby API service called ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927bfd25c552e06dcdd5b3f","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://schools.tom.so","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools.tom.so","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". It is running on a relatively simple stack of Cloudflare Workers, Drizzle, Hono, OpenAPI and SQLite. In a nutshell, it \"ingests\" the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1ce5c552e06dcdd5b48","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.educationcounts.govt.nz/directories/school-directory-api","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools directory dataset from the Ministry of Education","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" as a scheduled task and (re)serves this as a REST API.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Technically it is possible and perfectly fine to use the endpoints from data.govt.nz directly, but from past experience I''ve found that the performance can dramatically slow down or go offline completely. Also, the way they recommend acting with their API is kind of crazy:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"\"For instance, a request to: ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1},{"id":"6927c22e5c552e06dcdd5b49","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://catalogue.data.govt.nz/api/3/action/datastore_search_sql?sql=SELECT%20*%20FROM%224b292323-9fcc-41f8-814b-3c7b19cf14b3%22","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"https://catalogue.data.govt.nz/api/3/action/datastore_search_sql?sql=SELECT * FROM\"4b292323-9fcc-41f8-814b-3c7b19cf14b3\"","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textFormat":2},{"mode":"normal","text":" will return all rows and columns from the Schools Directory.\"","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Yes sir, that is a raw dog SQL query being made in the URL param lol. Although since this is an open data government portal, I suppose it makes sense to do it this way since most researchers would be used to a CKAN API/SQL. Who knows 🤷","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In any case, acting as a mirror on Cloudflare means that you immediately get all of the edge speed benefits out of the box with Workers, and using their KV store product also means that you can cache the responses as well (since it isn''t like new schools are coming online in New Zealand frequently). So, I opted to create this and have an OpenAPI spec generator running as well (comes out of the box with Hono).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This was all working nicely and without issue, but then I stumbled upon ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0285c552e06dcdd5b40","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stainless.com","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Stainless","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", an SDK generation service similar to Speakeasy that also offered MCP server support. I saw that the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0795c552e06dcdd5b42","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/sst/opencode-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"SST team","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0555c552e06dcdd5b41","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.terminal.shop/api#client-sdks","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"terminal.shop","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" were already using this for their multi-language SDKs, so I tried pointing it to my API service.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"As a complete normie and noob when it comes to building out your own SDK, let alone an MCP server, this was genuinely such a painless and smooth experience. So far I haven''t actually needed to pay anything, and have SDKs for ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0955c552e06dcdd5b43","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Typescript","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0b65c552e06dcdd5b45","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-php","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"PHP","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0a65c552e06dcdd5b44","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Python","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0d35c552e06dcdd5b46","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/schools-sdk-mcp","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"the MCP server","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" all running for free. The Stainless bot automatically creates PRs and releases in the respective repositories, but ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"I haven''t had to set any of this up myself","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":1,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The fact that this service is basically completely hands-off and language agnostic is huge in my opinion. I don''t know what the pricing is, but whatever it is I think it is fully worth it lol. Take a look at me asking my schools MCP to give me some facts about Takapuna Grammar School (my old place of work):","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927be197230e15de599443c","media":21,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"You can see it immediately recognises the tools that the MCP offers. I did not write any of these tools myself - Stainless has defined these based on my OpenAPI spec which outlines each endpoint and what it returns.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After a short while, it returns the basic facts that I asked for:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927bea87230e15de599443d","media":22,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This entire project took maybe a day to set up and get running, including all of the Cloudflare Workers deployment and the Stainless configuration. While the capabilities are still very simple, I think this could enable some really interesting and powerful workflows through the combination of data sources. For example, I could have my API service consume multiple datasets related to education, not just from data.govt.nz but from other sources, and then have an agent or LLM access one or more tools based on my natural language query to join and serve responses.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you want to give it a go, feel free to ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1125c552e06dcdd5b47","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript/tree/main/packages/mcp-server","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"follow the steps outlined in my MCP package doc","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". You should be able to add and interact with this using any modern editor or agent so long as you have Node installed. Despite it saying you need an API key this is not required at least at the moment, although it might change in the future if I start needing to serve more data sources (or things start getting costly). Otherwise, maybe try making your own!","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 'stainless-is-amazing', '2025-11-27T03:19:58.084Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.042Z', 'draft', '2025-11-27T02:41:51.378Z', '2025-11-27T03:19:58.084Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (72, 22, 'Stainless is amazing', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Recently I created a hobby API service called ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927bfd25c552e06dcdd5b3f","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://schools.tom.so","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools.tom.so","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". It is running on a relatively simple stack of Cloudflare Workers, Drizzle, Hono, OpenAPI and SQLite. In a nutshell, it \"ingests\" the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1ce5c552e06dcdd5b48","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.educationcounts.govt.nz/directories/school-directory-api","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools directory dataset from the Ministry of Education","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" as a scheduled task and (re)serves this as a REST API.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Technically it is possible and perfectly fine to use the endpoints from data.govt.nz directly, but from past experience I''ve found that the performance can dramatically slow down or go offline completely. Also, the way they recommend acting with their API is kind of crazy:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"\"For instance, a request to: ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1},{"id":"6927c22e5c552e06dcdd5b49","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://catalogue.data.govt.nz/api/3/action/datastore_search_sql?sql=SELECT%20*%20FROM%224b292323-9fcc-41f8-814b-3c7b19cf14b3%22","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"https://catalogue.data.govt.nz/api/3/action/datastore_search_sql?sql=SELECT * FROM\"4b292323-9fcc-41f8-814b-3c7b19cf14b3\"","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textFormat":2},{"mode":"normal","text":" will return all rows and columns from the Schools Directory.\"","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Yes sir, that is a raw dog SQL query being made in the URL param lol. Although since this is an open data government portal, I suppose it makes sense to do it this way since most researchers would be used to a CKAN API/SQL. Who knows 🤷","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In any case, acting as a mirror on Cloudflare means that you immediately get all of the edge speed benefits out of the box with Workers, and using their KV store product also means that you can cache the responses as well (since it isn''t like new schools are coming online in New Zealand frequently). So, I opted to create this and have an OpenAPI spec generator running as well (comes out of the box with Hono).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This was all working nicely and without issue, but then I stumbled upon ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0285c552e06dcdd5b40","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stainless.com","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Stainless","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", an SDK generation service similar to Speakeasy that also offered MCP server support. I saw that the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0795c552e06dcdd5b42","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/sst/opencode-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"SST team","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0555c552e06dcdd5b41","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.terminal.shop/api#client-sdks","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"terminal.shop","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" were already using this for their multi-language SDKs, so I tried pointing it to my API service.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"As a complete normie and noob when it comes to building out your own SDK, let alone an MCP server, this was genuinely such a painless and smooth experience. So far I haven''t actually needed to pay anything, and have SDKs for ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0955c552e06dcdd5b43","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Typescript","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0b65c552e06dcdd5b45","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-php","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"PHP","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0a65c552e06dcdd5b44","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Python","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0d35c552e06dcdd5b46","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/schools-sdk-mcp","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"the MCP server","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" all running for free. The Stainless bot automatically creates PRs and releases in the respective repositories, but ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"I haven''t had to set any of this up myself","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":1,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The fact that this service is basically completely hands-off and language agnostic is huge in my opinion. I don''t know what the pricing is, but whatever it is I think it is fully worth it lol. Take a look at me asking my schools MCP to give me some facts about Takapuna Grammar School (my old place of work):","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927be197230e15de599443c","media":21,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"You can see it immediately recognises the tools that the MCP offers. I did not write any of these tools myself - Stainless has defined these based on my OpenAPI spec which outlines each endpoint and what it returns.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After a short while, it returns the basic facts that I asked for:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927bea87230e15de599443d","media":22,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This entire project took maybe a day to set up and get running, including all of the Cloudflare Workers deployment and the Stainless configuration. While the capabilities are still very simple, I think this could enable some really interesting and powerful workflows through the combination of data sources. For example, I could have my API service consume multiple datasets related to education, not just from data.govt.nz but from other sources, and then have an agent or LLM access one or more tools based on my natural language query to join and serve responses.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you want to give it a go, feel free to ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1125c552e06dcdd5b47","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript/tree/main/packages/mcp-server","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"follow the steps outlined in my MCP package doc","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". You should be able to add and interact with this using any modern editor or agent so long as you have Node installed. Despite it saying you need an API key this is not required at least at the moment, although it might change in the future if I start needing to serve more data sources (or things start getting costly). Otherwise, maybe try making your own!","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-11-27T03:00:00.000Z', 0, 'stainless-is-amazing', '2025-11-27T03:20:10.458Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.042Z', 'published', '2025-11-27T03:20:10.489Z', '2025-11-27T03:20:10.489Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (73, 22, 'Stainless is amazing', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Recently I created a hobby API service called ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927bfd25c552e06dcdd5b3f","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://schools.tom.so","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools.tom.so","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". It is running on a relatively simple stack of Cloudflare Workers, Drizzle, Hono, OpenAPI and SQLite. In a nutshell, it \"ingests\" the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1ce5c552e06dcdd5b48","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.educationcounts.govt.nz/directories/school-directory-api","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools directory dataset from the Ministry of Education","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" as a scheduled task and (re)serves this as a REST API.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Technically it is possible and perfectly fine to use the endpoints from data.govt.nz directly, but from past experience I''ve found that the performance can dramatically slow down or go offline completely. Also, the way they recommend acting with their API is kind of crazy:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927c3f441837d2e199b65b6","media":23,"blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Yes sir, that is a raw dog SQL query being made in the URL param lol. I get that being able to do SQL joins between tables in their datastore via HTTP would be useful, especially since this is an open data government portal aimed at researchers would be used to a CKAN API/SQL... but who knows 🤷","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In any case, acting as a mirror on Cloudflare means that you immediately get all of the edge speed benefits out of the box with Workers, and using their KV store product also means that you can cache the responses as well (since it isn''t like new schools are coming online in New Zealand frequently). So, I opted to create this and have an OpenAPI spec generator running as well (comes out of the box with Hono).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This was all working nicely and without issue, but then I stumbled upon ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0285c552e06dcdd5b40","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stainless.com","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Stainless","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", an SDK generation service similar to Speakeasy that also offered MCP server support. I saw that the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0795c552e06dcdd5b42","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/sst/opencode-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"SST team","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0555c552e06dcdd5b41","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.terminal.shop/api#client-sdks","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"terminal.shop","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" were already using this for their multi-language SDKs, so I tried pointing it to my API service.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"As a complete normie and noob when it comes to building out your own SDK, let alone an MCP server, this was genuinely such a painless and smooth experience. So far I haven''t actually needed to pay anything, and have SDKs for ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0955c552e06dcdd5b43","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Typescript","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0b65c552e06dcdd5b45","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-php","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"PHP","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0a65c552e06dcdd5b44","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Python","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0d35c552e06dcdd5b46","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/schools-sdk-mcp","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"the MCP server","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" all running for free. The Stainless bot automatically creates PRs and releases in the respective repositories, but ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"I haven''t had to set any of this up myself","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":1,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The fact that this service is basically completely hands-off and language agnostic is huge in my opinion. I don''t know what the pricing is, but whatever it is I think it is fully worth it lol. Take a look at me asking my schools MCP to give me some facts about Takapuna Grammar School (my old place of work):","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927be197230e15de599443c","media":21,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"You can see it immediately recognises the tools that the MCP offers. I did not write any of these tools myself - Stainless has defined these based on my OpenAPI spec which outlines each endpoint and what it returns.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After a short while, it returns the basic facts that I asked for:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927bea87230e15de599443d","media":22,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This entire project took maybe a day to set up and get running, including all of the Cloudflare Workers deployment and the Stainless configuration. While the capabilities are still very simple, I think this could enable some really interesting and powerful workflows through the combination of data sources. For example, I could have my API service consume multiple datasets related to education, not just from data.govt.nz but from other sources, and then have an agent or LLM access one or more tools based on my natural language query to join and serve responses.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you want to give it a go, feel free to ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1125c552e06dcdd5b47","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript/tree/main/packages/mcp-server","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"follow the steps outlined in my MCP package doc","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". You should be able to add and interact with this using any modern editor or agent so long as you have Node installed. Despite it saying you need an API key this is not required at least at the moment, although it might change in the future if I start needing to serve more data sources (or things start getting costly). Otherwise, maybe try making your own!","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-11-27T03:00:00.000Z', 0, 'stainless-is-amazing', '2025-11-27T03:24:02.668Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.042Z', 'draft', '2025-11-27T03:22:34.122Z', '2025-11-27T03:24:02.668Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (74, 22, 'Stainless is amazing', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Recently I created a hobby API service called ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927bfd25c552e06dcdd5b3f","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://schools.tom.so","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools.tom.so","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". It is running on a relatively simple stack of Cloudflare Workers, Drizzle, Hono, OpenAPI and SQLite. In a nutshell, it \"ingests\" the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1ce5c552e06dcdd5b48","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.educationcounts.govt.nz/directories/school-directory-api","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools directory dataset from the Ministry of Education","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" as a scheduled task and (re)serves this as a REST API.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Technically it is possible and perfectly fine to use the endpoints from data.govt.nz directly, but from past experience I''ve found that the performance can dramatically slow down or go offline completely. Also, the way they recommend acting with their API is kind of crazy:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927c3f441837d2e199b65b6","media":23,"blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Yes sir, that is a raw dog SQL query being made in the URL param lol. I get that being able to do SQL joins between tables in their datastore via HTTP would be useful, especially since this is an open data government portal aimed at researchers would be used to a CKAN API/SQL... but who knows 🤷","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In any case, acting as a mirror on Cloudflare means that you immediately get all of the edge speed benefits out of the box with Workers, and using their KV store product also means that you can cache the responses as well (since it isn''t like new schools are coming online in New Zealand frequently). So, I opted to create this and have an OpenAPI spec generator running as well (comes out of the box with Hono).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This was all working nicely and without issue, but then I stumbled upon ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0285c552e06dcdd5b40","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stainless.com","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Stainless","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", an SDK generation service similar to Speakeasy that also offered MCP server support. I saw that the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0795c552e06dcdd5b42","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/sst/opencode-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"SST team","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0555c552e06dcdd5b41","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.terminal.shop/api#client-sdks","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"terminal.shop","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" were already using this for their multi-language SDKs, so I tried pointing it to my API service.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"As a complete normie and noob when it comes to building out your own SDK, let alone an MCP server, this was genuinely such a painless and smooth experience. So far I haven''t actually needed to pay anything, and have SDKs for ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0955c552e06dcdd5b43","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Typescript","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0b65c552e06dcdd5b45","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-php","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"PHP","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0a65c552e06dcdd5b44","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Python","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0d35c552e06dcdd5b46","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/schools-sdk-mcp","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"the MCP server","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" all running for free. The Stainless bot automatically creates PRs and releases in the respective repositories, but ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"I haven''t had to set any of this up myself","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":1,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The fact that this service is basically completely hands-off and language agnostic is huge in my opinion. I don''t know what the pricing is, but whatever it is I think it is fully worth it lol. Take a look at me asking my schools MCP to give me some facts about Takapuna Grammar School (my old place of work):","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927be197230e15de599443c","media":21,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"You can see it immediately recognises the tools that the MCP offers. I did not write any of these tools myself - Stainless has defined these based on my OpenAPI spec which outlines each endpoint and what it returns.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After a short while, it returns the basic facts that I asked for:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927bea87230e15de599443d","media":22,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This entire project took maybe a day to set up and get running, including all of the Cloudflare Workers deployment and the Stainless configuration. While the capabilities are still very simple, I think this could enable some really interesting and powerful workflows through the combination of data sources. For example, I could have my API service consume multiple datasets related to education, not just from data.govt.nz but from other sources, and then have an agent or LLM access one or more tools based on my natural language query to join and serve responses.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you want to give it a go, feel free to ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1125c552e06dcdd5b47","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript/tree/main/packages/mcp-server","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"follow the steps outlined in my MCP package doc","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". You should be able to add and interact with this using any modern editor or agent so long as you have Node installed. Despite it saying you need an API key this is not required at least at the moment, although it might change in the future if I start needing to serve more data sources (or things start getting costly). Otherwise, maybe try making your own!","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-11-27T03:00:00.000Z', 0, 'stainless-is-amazing', '2025-11-27T03:24:04.867Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.042Z', 'published', '2025-11-27T03:24:04.886Z', '2025-11-27T03:24:04.886Z', 0, 0);
