ally slow down or go offline completely. Also, the way they recommend acting with their API is kind of crazy:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927c3f441837d2e199b65b6","media":23,"blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Yes sir, that is a raw dog SQL query being made in the URL param lol. I get that being able to do SQL joins between tables in their datastore via HTTP would be useful, especially since this is an open data government portal aimed at researchers would be used to a CKAN API/SQL... but who knows 🤷","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In any case, acting as a mirror on Cloudflare means that you immediately get all of the edge speed benefits out of the box with Workers, and using their KV store product also means that you can cache the responses as well (since it isn''t like new schools are coming online in New Zealand frequently). So, I opted to create this and have an OpenAPI spec generator running as well (comes out of the box with Hono).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This was all working nicely and without issue, but then I stumbled upon ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0285c552e06dcdd5b40","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stainless.com","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Stainless","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", an SDK generation service similar to Speakeasy that also offered MCP server support. I saw that the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0795c552e06dcdd5b42","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/sst/opencode-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"SST team","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0555c552e06dcdd5b41","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.terminal.shop/api#client-sdks","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"terminal.shop","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" were already using this for their multi-language SDKs, so I tried pointing it to my API service.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"As a complete normie and noob when it comes to building out your own SDK, let alone an MCP server, this was genuinely such a painless and smooth experience. So far I haven''t actually needed to pay anything, and have SDKs for ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0955c552e06dcdd5b43","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Typescript","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0b65c552e06dcdd5b45","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-php","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"PHP","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0a65c552e06dcdd5b44","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Python","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0d35c552e06dcdd5b46","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/schools-sdk-mcp","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"the MCP server","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" all running for free. The Stainless bot automatically creates PRs and releases in the respective repositories, but ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"I haven''t had to set any of this up myself","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":1,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The fact that this service is basically completely hands-off and language agnostic is huge in my opinion. I don''t know what the pricing is, but whatever it is I think it is fully worth it lol. Take a look at me asking my schools MCP to give me some facts about Takapuna Grammar School (my old place of work):","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927be197230e15de599443c","media":21,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"You can see it immediately recognises the tools that the MCP offers. I did not write any of these tools myself - Stainless has defined these based on my OpenAPI spec which outlines each endpoint and what it returns.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After a short while, it returns the basic facts that I asked for:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927bea87230e15de599443d","media":22,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This entire project took maybe a day to set up and get running, including all of the Cloudflare Workers deployment and the Stainless configuration. While the capabilities are still very simple, I think this could enable some really interesting and powerful workflows through the combination of data sources. For example, I could have my API service consume multiple datasets related to education, not just from data.govt.nz but from other sources, and then have an agent or LLM access one or more tools based on my natural language query to join and serve responses.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you want to give it a go, feel free to ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1125c552e06dcdd5b47","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript/tree/main/packages/mcp-server","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"follow the steps outlined in my MCP package doc","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". You should be able to add and interact with this using any modern editor or agent so long as you have Node installed. Despite it saying you need an API key this is not required at least at the moment, although it might change in the future if I start needing to serve more data sources (or things start getting costly). Otherwise, maybe try making your own!","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Stainless is amazing', NULL, 'Or, how I built a toy MCP server', '2025-11-27T03:00:00.000Z', 0, 'stainless-is-amazing', '2025-11-27T03:26:12.125Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.042Z', 'published', '2025-11-27T03:26:12.141Z', '2025-11-27T03:26:12.141Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (77, 22, 'Stainless is amazing', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Recently I created a hobby API service called ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927bfd25c552e06dcdd5b3f","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://schools.tom.so","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools.tom.so","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". It is running on a relatively simple stack of Cloudflare Workers, Drizzle, Hono, OpenAPI and SQLite. In a nutshell, it \"ingests\" the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1ce5c552e06dcdd5b48","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.educationcounts.govt.nz/directories/school-directory-api","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"schools directory dataset from the Ministry of Education","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" as a scheduled task and (re)serves this as a REST API.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Technically it is possible and perfectly fine to use the endpoints from data.govt.nz directly, but from past experience I''ve found that the performance can dramatically slow down or go offline completely. Also, the way they recommend acting with their API is kind of crazy:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927c3f441837d2e199b65b6","media":23,"blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Yes sir, that is a raw dog SQL query being made in the URL param lol. I get that being able to do SQL joins between tables in their datastore via HTTP would be useful, especially since this is an open data government portal aimed at researchers would be used to a CKAN API/SQL... but who knows 🤷","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"In any case, acting as a mirror on Cloudflare means that you immediately get all of the edge speed benefits out of the box with Workers, and using their KV store product also means that you can cache the responses as well (since it isn''t like new schools are coming online in New Zealand frequently). So, I opted to create this and have an OpenAPI spec generator running as well (comes out of the box with Hono).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This was all working nicely and without issue, but then I stumbled upon ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0285c552e06dcdd5b40","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://stainless.com","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Stainless","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", an SDK generation service similar to Speakeasy that also offered MCP server support. I saw that the ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0795c552e06dcdd5b42","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/sst/opencode-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"SST team","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0555c552e06dcdd5b41","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.terminal.shop/api#client-sdks","linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"terminal.shop","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" were already using this for their multi-language SDKs, so I tried pointing it to my API service.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"As a complete normie and noob when it comes to building out your own SDK, let alone an MCP server, this was genuinely such a painless and smooth experience. So far I haven''t actually needed to pay anything, and have SDKs for ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0955c552e06dcdd5b43","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Typescript","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0b65c552e06dcdd5b45","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-php","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"PHP","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0a65c552e06dcdd5b44","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-python","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Python","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":", and ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c0d35c552e06dcdd5b46","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/schools-sdk-mcp","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"the MCP server","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" all running for free. The Stainless bot automatically creates PRs and releases in the respective repositories, but ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"I haven''t had to set any of this up myself","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":1,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":".","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The fact that this service is basically completely hands-off and language agnostic is huge in my opinion. I don''t know what the pricing is, but whatever it is I think it is fully worth it lol. Take a look at me asking my schools MCP to give me some facts about Takapuna Grammar School (my old place of work):","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927be197230e15de599443c","media":21,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"You can see it immediately recognises the tools that the MCP offers. I did not write any of these tools myself - Stainless has defined these based on my OpenAPI spec which outlines each endpoint and what it returns.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"After a short while, it returns the basic facts that I asked for:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"6927bea87230e15de599443d","media":22,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This entire project took maybe a day to set up and get running, including all of the Cloudflare Workers deployment and the Stainless configuration. While the capabilities are still very simple, I think this could enable some really interesting and powerful workflows through the combination of data sources. For example, I could have my API service consume multiple datasets related to education, not just from data.govt.nz but from other sources, and then have an agent or LLM access one or more tools based on my natural language query to join and serve responses.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you want to give it a go, feel free to ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"6927c1125c552e06dcdd5b47","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://github.com/et0and/schools-sdk-typescript/tree/main/packages/mcp-server","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"follow the steps outlined in my MCP package doc","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". You should be able to add and interact with this using any modern editor or agent so long as you have Node installed. Despite it saying you need an API key this is not required at least at the moment, although it might change in the future if I start needing to serve more data sources (or things start getting costly). Otherwise, maybe try making your own!","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Stainless is amazing', NULL, 'How I built a toy MCP server with Stainless', '2025-11-27T03:00:00.000Z', 0, 'stainless-is-amazing', '2025-11-27T03:26:29.587Z', '2025-11-27T02:41:16.042Z', 'published', '2025-11-27T03:26:29.602Z', '2025-11-27T03:26:29.602Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (78, 23, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-13T09:34:52.494Z', '2025-12-13T09:34:52.493Z', 'draft', '2025-12-13T09:34:52.521Z', '2025-12-13T09:34:52.521Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (79, 23, 'Writing with AI is a cop out', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"By now it’s pretty much everywhere, but I’ve started to get a very good eye for spotting when some piece of content has been written by AI. It doesn’t matter what the model is, if it’s the new SOTA of OpenAI/Anthropic/Google/Meta or whatever. They all sound like shit and it’s obvious. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Case in point, there is a very large number of “people” on Twitter/X who have LLM replies. In some cases these will be bots, but I actually suspect that there’s a high number of people that literally defer their thoughts and opinions to some AI browser plugin. I started seeing it mostly across tech accounts, but you tend to see it everywhere now. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"693d33daa7bbb89525abc79e","media":25,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"What do you gain from outsourcing your literal ability to think to an LLM? Writing is inherently messy and difficult if you are trying to express some idea, but that’s precisely the point. It is meant to be hard because it forces you to think and validate your thoughts in a way that others, including yourself, can structure and comprehend in some shape, way or form. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you prompt an LLM that in itself is a form of writing that requires thought and consideration. You need to structure your thought in such a way that it can be comprehended by the LLM, which would likely also mean it is understandable to other humans too. But in the case of that reply to Dax’s post above I’m convinced the user didn’t even prompt the LLM. At most of they might’ve said something like “write a response to this tweet”. What the fuck is the point?","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I’ve seen more examples at work too where commit messages are AI, PR titles and descriptions are AI, the code itself is AI, and any comments in said code is also AI. At most you’ve probably prompted the code itself, but everything else you’ve click opsed within VS Code and GitHub with their AI generation features. There’s then a very high chance of it basically being complete slop all the way down. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The transformer architecture of an LLM inherently makes it such that you can never be “creative” by it alone. An AI bot is empty insofar as it just produces a pattern of some kind, but this in isolation isn’t that malicious. No, what’s more insidious is when there are still living and breathing humans that simply hit “publish” without any other engagement. This is worse than dead internet theory. How does that make you any different from said machine then? Doing this means you’ve given up and surrendered your ability to engage with the world in a meaningful way.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I’ve become so conditioned by encountering these things that I second guess myself now when I write. I genuinely will edit something I’ve written because I think it “sounds too AI”, and avoid the use of emdashes and hyphens for the same reason. If a paragraph is around 3 sentences long (this is how I was taught in university), I think the structure “looks like AI” as I’ve observed LLMs have a tendency of sticking with shorter paragraphs rather than long ones. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I couldn’t imagine being a teenager going through highschool now, let alone being a teacher. When I left teaching GPT 4 was considered the most powerful model, but it was far from a mainstream technology and before everything became an “agent”.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Aristotle refers to a term called “lógos” which roughly translates to word, discourse or reason. That is, the written word means one’s ability to formulate their own thinking, understanding and order. This is all very philosophical, but it is also deeply rooted in human psychology insofar as our ability to write is a ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"693d3391a7bbb89525abc79d","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://summit.sfu.ca/item/2296","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"primary driver of our cognitive development","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" (particularly in children).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"LLMs are cool sure. I’ve used them a lot particularly this past year to brainstorm, debug and learn as a developer. But I would never want to voluntarily make myself an empty mouthpiece for an LLM. Doing so is the equivalent of unplugging my brain completely for some memetic machine that is far, far from actual intelligence. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Writing with AI is a cop out', NULL, 'It sounds like shit and it’s obvious', '2025-12-13T09:00:00.000Z', 0, 'writing-with-ai-is-a-cop-out', '2025-12-13T09:50:52.959Z', '2025-12-13T09:34:52.493Z', 'draft', '2025-12-13T09:35:08.263Z', '2025-12-13T09:50:52.959Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (80, 23, 'Writing with AI is a cop out', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"By now it’s pretty much everywhere, but I’ve started to get a very good eye for spotting when some piece of content has been written by AI. It doesn’t matter what the model is, if it’s the new SOTA of OpenAI/Anthropic/Google/Meta or whatever. They all sound like shit and it’s obvious. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Case in point, there is a very large number of “people” on Twitter/X who have LLM replies. In some cases these will be bots, but I actually suspect that there’s a high number of people that literally defer their thoughts and opinions to some AI browser plugin. I started seeing it mostly across tech accounts, but you tend to see it everywhere now. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"693d33daa7bbb89525abc79e","media":25,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"What do you gain from outsourcing your literal ability to think to an LLM? Writing is inherently messy and difficult if you are trying to express some idea, but that’s precisely the point. It is meant to be hard because it forces you to think and validate your thoughts in a way that others, including yourself, can structure and comprehend in some shape, way or form. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you prompt an LLM that in itself is a form of writing that requires thought and consideration. You need to structure your thought in such a way that it can be comprehended by the LLM, which would likely also mean it is understandable to other humans too. But in the case of that reply to Dax’s post above I’m convinced the user didn’t even prompt the LLM. At most of they might’ve said something like “write a response to this tweet”. What the fuck is the point?","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I’ve seen more examples at work too where commit messages are AI, PR titles and descriptions are AI, the code itself is AI, and any comments in said code is also AI. At most you’ve probably prompted the code itself, but everything else you’ve click opsed within VS Code and GitHub with their AI generation features. There’s then a very high chance of it basically being complete slop all the way down. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The transformer architecture of an LLM inherently makes it such that you can never be “creative” by it alone. An AI bot is empty insofar as it just produces a pattern of some kind, but this in isolation isn’t that malicious. No, what’s more insidious is when there are still living and breathing humans that simply hit “publish” without any other engagement. This is worse than dead internet theory. How does that make you any different from said machine then? Doing this means you’ve given up and surrendered your ability to engage with the world in a meaningful way.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I’ve become so conditioned by encountering these things that I second guess myself now when I write. I genuinely will edit something I’ve written because I think it “sounds too AI”, and avoid the use of emdashes and hyphens for the same reason. If a paragraph is around 3 sentences long (this is how I was taught in university), I think the structure “looks like AI” as I’ve observed LLMs have a tendency of sticking with shorter paragraphs rather than long ones. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I couldn’t imagine being a teenager going through highschool now, let alone being a teacher. When I left teaching GPT 4 was considered the most powerful model, but it was far from a mainstream technology and before everything became an “agent”.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Aristotle refers to a term called “lógos” which roughly translates to word, discourse or reason. That is, the written word means one’s ability to formulate their own thinking, understanding and order. This is all very philosophical, but it is also deeply rooted in human psychology insofar as our ability to write is a ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"693d3391a7bbb89525abc79d","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://summit.sfu.ca/item/2296","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"primary driver of our cognitive development","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" (particularly in children).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"LLMs are cool sure. I’ve used them a lot particularly this past year to brainstorm, debug and learn as a developer. But I would never want to voluntarily make myself an empty mouthpiece for an LLM. Doing so is the equivalent of unplugging my brain completely for some memetic machine that is far, far from actual intelligence. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Writing with AI is a cop out', NULL, 'It sounds like shit and it’s obvious', '2025-12-13T09:00:00.000Z', 0, 'writing-with-ai-is-a-cop-out', '2025-12-13T09:50:56.695Z', '2025-12-13T09:34:52.493Z', 'published', '2025-12-13T09:50:56.717Z', '2025-12-13T09:50:56.717Z', 0, 0);
