ete slop all the way down. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The transformer architecture of an LLM inherently makes it such that you can never be “creative” by it alone. An AI bot is empty insofar as it just produces a pattern of some kind, but this in isolation isn’t that malicious. No, what’s more insidious is when there are still living and breathing humans that simply hit “publish” without any other engagement. This is worse than dead internet theory. How does that make you any different from said machine then? Doing this means you’ve given up and surrendered your ability to engage with the world in a meaningful way.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I’ve become so conditioned by encountering these things that I second guess myself now when I write. I genuinely will edit something I’ve written because I think it “sounds too AI”, and avoid the use of emdashes and hyphens for the same reason. If a paragraph is around 3 sentences long (this is how I was taught in university), I think the structure “looks like AI” as I’ve observed LLMs have a tendency of sticking with shorter paragraphs rather than long ones. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Aristotle refers to a term called “lógos” which roughly translates to word, discourse or reason. That is, the written word means one’s ability to formulate their own thinking, understanding and order. This is all very philosophical, but it is also deeply rooted in human psychology insofar as our ability to write is a ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"693d3391a7bbb89525abc79d","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://summit.sfu.ca/item/2296","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"primary driver of our cognitive development","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" (particularly in children). This makes our ability to write something deeply human and very real. It isn’t just language that instills and gives form to true intelligence but our means of shaping it via the written word. Give this up and we are ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"LLMs are cool sure. I’ve used them a lot particularly this past year to brainstorm, debug and learn as a developer. But I would never want to voluntarily make myself an empty mouthpiece for an LLM. Doing so is the equivalent of unplugging my brain completely for some memetic machine that is far, far from actual intelligence. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Writing with AI is a cop out', NULL, 'It sounds like shit and it’s obvious', '2025-12-13T09:00:00.000Z', 0, 'writing-with-ai-is-a-cop-out', '2025-12-13T10:08:25.347Z', '2025-12-13T09:34:52.493Z', 'draft', '2025-12-13T10:04:41.299Z', '2025-12-13T10:08:25.347Z', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (83, 23, 'Writing with AI is a cop out', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"By now it’s pretty much everywhere, but I’ve started to get a very good eye for spotting when some piece of content has been written by AI. It doesn’t matter what the model is, if it’s the new SOTA of OpenAI/Anthropic/Google/Meta or whatever. They all sound like shit and it’s obvious. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Case in point, there is a very large number of “people” on Twitter/X who have LLM replies. In some cases these will be bots, but I actually suspect that there’s a high number of people that literally defer their thoughts and opinions to some AI browser plugin. I started seeing it mostly across tech accounts, but you tend to see it everywhere now. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"693d33daa7bbb89525abc79e","media":25,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"What do you gain from outsourcing your literal ability to think to an LLM? Writing is inherently messy and difficult if you are trying to express some idea, but that’s precisely the point. It is meant to be hard because it forces you to think and validate your thoughts in a way that others, including yourself, can structure and comprehend in some shape, way or form. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"If you prompt an LLM that in itself is a form of writing that requires thought and consideration. You need to structure your thought in such a way that it can be comprehended by the LLM, which would likely also mean it is understandable to other humans too. But in the case of that reply to Dax’s post above I’m convinced the user didn’t even prompt the LLM. At most of they might’ve said something like “write a response to this tweet”. What the fuck is the point?","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I’ve seen more examples at work too where commit messages are AI, PR titles and descriptions are AI, the code itself is AI, and any comments in said code is also AI. At most you’ve probably prompted the code itself, but everything else you’ve click opsed within VS Code and GitHub with their AI generation features. There’s then a very high chance of it basically being complete slop all the way down. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The transformer architecture of an LLM inherently makes it such that you can never be “creative” by it alone. An AI bot is empty insofar as it just produces a pattern of some kind, but this in isolation isn’t that malicious. No, what’s more insidious is when there are still living and breathing humans that simply hit “publish” without any other engagement. This is worse than dead internet theory. How does that make you any different from said machine then? Doing this means you’ve given up and surrendered your ability to engage with the world in a meaningful way.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I’ve become so conditioned by encountering these things that I second guess myself now when I write. I genuinely will edit something I’ve written because I think it “sounds too AI”, and avoid the use of emdashes and hyphens for the same reason. If a paragraph is around 3 sentences long (this is how I was taught in university), I think the structure “looks like AI” as I’ve observed LLMs have a tendency of sticking with shorter paragraphs rather than long ones. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Aristotle refers to a term called “lógos” which roughly translates to word, discourse or reason. That is, the written word means one’s ability to formulate their own thinking, understanding and order. This is all very philosophical, but it is also deeply rooted in human psychology insofar as our ability to write is a ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"693d3391a7bbb89525abc79d","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://summit.sfu.ca/item/2296","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"primary driver of our cognitive development","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" (particularly in children). This makes our ability to write something deeply human and very real. It isn’t just language that instills and gives form to true intelligence but our means of shaping it via the written word. Give this up and we are potentially throwing away a core tenet of what makes us human…","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"start","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"LLMs are cool sure. I’ve used them a lot particularly this past year to brainstorm, debug and learn as a developer. But I would never want to voluntarily make myself an empty mouthpiece for an LLM. Doing so is the equivalent of unplugging my brain completely for some memetic machine that is far, far from actual intelligence. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'Writing with AI is a cop out', NULL, 'It sounds like shit and it’s obvious', '2025-12-13T09:00:00.000Z', 0, 'writing-with-ai-is-a-cop-out', '2025-12-13T10:08:55.606Z', '2025-12-13T09:34:52.493Z', 'published', '2025-12-13T10:08:55.638Z', '2025-12-13T10:08:55.638Z', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (84, 24, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-06T00:12:09.566Z', '2026-01-06T00:12:09.564Z', 'draft', '2026-01-06T00:12:09.583Z', '2026-01-06T00:12:09.583Z', 0, 0);
INSERT INTO "_posts_v" ("id", "parent_id", "version_title", "version_hero_image_id", "version_content", "version_meta_title", "version_meta_image_id", "version_meta_description", "version_published_at", "version_generate_slug", "version_slug", "version_updated_at", "version_created_at", "version__status", "created_at", "updated_at", "latest", "autosave") VALUES (85, 24, 'People deserve better', NULL, '{"root":{"type":"root","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Over the Christmas and New Year period here in New Zealand, one of the largest and widely used healthcare portals used by doctors and health centres ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"695c545acaf42b7e1bbbd723","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/national/583248/manage-my-health-data-breach-ransom-deadline-arrives","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"got hacked","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":". 108GiB worth of personal health data, including (in some cases) passport scans, prescription information, names, addresses, NHI numbers etc from this Manage My Health (MMH). Initially the group responsible (Kazu) asked for a 300K ransom, but then lowered this to 60K in an effort to try and force MMH''s hand.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"block","fields":{"id":"695c54b2caf42b7e1bbbd724","media":26,"blockName":"","blockType":"mediaBlock"},"format":"","version":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"MMH has basically been completely silent since the hack was made public. Most health practices found out about the breach via media outlets, and only after repeated attempts to contact MMH failed so Kazu then posted a sample of the hacked data. It is unclear how the breach happened, if the exploit has since been fixed, who exactly has been affected and how long the vulnerability has existed in the MMH portal.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"While the government is chasing it''s tail launching all sorts of different reviews and injunctions, much of this in my opinion is focusing on the wrong questions. It is unacceptable for a ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":"HEALTHCARE","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1},{"mode":"normal","text":" SaaS platform to not have SOC 2 compliance and basic opsec at a minimum. They should be as secure as financial services like banks, if not more secure. Given how many health centres use MMH as a way for patients to manage prescription repeats, bookings etc, it is unfair for normal everyday people who have been pushed to use this shitty platform only to have their data mishandled.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Their ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"695c5780caf42b7e1bbbd725","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://archive.is/6VGLs","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"security page is incredibly vague","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" and just talks about SSL certificates. It doesn''t specify anything like where the data is stored, how it is stored (encrypted at rest, in transit, etc), if MMH undertake security audits, and instead just talks about how they have certs from GoDaddy (lol) and for the user to use antivirus on their computer. This should have been a massive red flag to anyone with a modicum of computer security knowledge looking to procure their services.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"The fact that MMH somehow became the preferred healthcare portal in New Zealand is insane to me. They haven''t apologised about the breach and instead are putting out the weakest damage control. This is clearly a massive fuck up on their part. From ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"695c5a9acaf42b7e1bbbd726","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7413120799634743296/","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"a recent LinkedIn post they state","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":":","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"\"The investigation has identified that one module, Health Documents, within the app was compromised, not the entire app. Manage My Health is commencing legal action to protect client data.\"","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Based on what I''ve read and inferred, this \"module\" was essentially a fuck up with how they set up Azure Blob storage where all documents and attachments were stored. I''m not going to post the exact source here, but some searches on Twitter will bring up posts that show this may well be the case. So this has likely been public for a very long time before Kazu even came across it.","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"I also found the following point from MMH very rich:","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"\"Manage My Health has [...] Re-secured all health documents and strengthened document storage controls.\"","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":2,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":2},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Bro, you cannot \"re-secure\" documents that were publicly accessible. They were not \"secure\" in the first place, so at most you are fixing access to the blob storage/bucket but the files themselves are wide open and fucked now. Also, nagging your users on making sure they have secure passwords and 2FA is meaningless if you can''t secure your own infra. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"This is shaping up to be one of the worst cybersecurity breaches in New Zealand and so far it appears that no one will be having to face the music. It is a failure on MMH''s part, but it is a wider signal showing the poor state of the system itself and its shitty standards. ","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1},{"id":"695c5b6dcaf42b7e1bbbd727","type":"link","fields":{"url":"https://www.openaccess.nz/blog/managemyhealth-hack-a-failure-of-standards/","newTab":true,"linkType":"custom"},"format":"","indent":0,"version":3,"children":[{"mode":"normal","text":"Callum McMenamin has written an excellent account of this","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null},{"mode":"normal","text":" that goes over this in great detail. Self-attestation is a massive issue with vendors - we need a legal standard that companies need to follow to ensure the secure handling of user data, and if not then appropriate fines and/or jail (seriously).","type":"text","style":"","detail":0,"format":0,"version":1}],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0},{"type":"paragraph","format":"","indent":0,"version":1,"children":[],"direction":null,"textStyle":"","textFormat":0}],"direction":null}}', 'People deserve better', NULL, 'Some thoughts on the recent Manage My Health hack', '2026-01-05T22:30:00.000Z', 1, 'people-deserve-better', '2026-01-06T00:54:12.662Z', '2026-01-06T00:12:09.564Z', 'draft', '2026-01-06T00:12:38.987Z', '2026-01-06T00:54:12.662Z', 0, 1);
